NAME
    gcloud alpha fault-testing experiments - manage Experiment resources

SYNOPSIS
    gcloud alpha fault-testing experiments GROUP | COMMAND
        [GCLOUD_WIDE_FLAG ...]

DESCRIPTION
    (ALPHA) Manage Experiment resources.

GCLOUD WIDE FLAGS
    These flags are available to all commands: --help.

    Run $ gcloud help for details.

GROUPS
    GROUP is one of the following:

     affected-resources
        (ALPHA) Manage Affected Resource resources.

COMMANDS
    COMMAND is one of the following:

     create
        (ALPHA) Create an experiment.

     delete
        (ALPHA) Delete an experiment.

     describe
        (ALPHA) Describe a current or past experiment.

     list
        (ALPHA) List current or past experiments.

     start
        (ALPHA) Start a new experiment run.

     stop
        (ALPHA) Cancel a running experiment.

     stop-all
        (ALPHA) Cancel all experiments in a given location.

NOTES
    This command is currently in alpha and might change without notice. If this
    command fails with API permission errors despite specifying the correct
    project, you might be trying to access an API with an invitation-only early
    access allowlist.

